1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Are you good with your hands?
你动手能力强吗？

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:08,440
Many of us like to make things which we can use or give as gifts.
我们很多人都喜欢制作一些可以自用或是当作礼物赠送的物件。

3
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:17,690
Crafting is certainly a hobby that’s seen a resurgence, and those who pursue it claim getting creative improves their mood.
爱好手工制作的风潮再次兴起，而那些投身其中的人表示，发挥创造力能让心情变得更好。

4
00:00:17,690 --> 00:00:27,660
The recent lockdowns caused by the Covid pandemic gave people time at home to try out new activities, which they’ve continued to enjoy.
最近由新冠疫情所引发的封锁，让人们有了居家时间去尝试新活动，而这些活动也被大家一直延续了下来。

5
00:00:27,660 --> 00:00:34,480
Many turned to hobbies such as craft making as a way to soothe their work-from-home burnout.
许多人选择手工制作这类爱好来缓解居家办公带来的倦怠感。

6
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:44,880
Knitting, crocheting, pottery and painting are all crafts that have seen a revival, and many of them are being done by younger people.
编织、钩针、陶艺和绘画这些手工技艺都迎来了复兴，并且其中不少爱好者都是年轻人。

7
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:55,470
But even before the pandemic, people were turning to arts and crafts as an interesting pastime and even a way to make a bit of pocket money.
但其实在疫情之前，人们就已经将手工艺当作一种有趣的消遣方式，甚至是赚点零花钱的途径了。

8
00:00:55,470 --> 00:01:02,750
Numerous websites, such as Etsy and Folksy, allowed people to sell their handmade goods.
像爱Etsy和Folksy这样的众多网站，都为人们售卖手工制品提供了平台。

9
00:01:02,750 --> 00:01:15,180
Richard Sennett, author of the Craftsman, told the BBC that: “A lot of people are finding their day jobs pretty empty, whereas learning a craft provides a real satisfaction.
《匠人》一书的作者理查德·桑内特在接受BBC采访时表示：“很多人觉得自己的日常工作十分空虚，而学习一门手艺却能带来实实在在的满足感。

10
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:25,990
It’s a skill – things like carpentry and weaving are mentally and physically stimulating, and people get inherent pleasure out of that kind of work”.
这是一种技能——像木工和编织这类手艺，既能锻炼脑力，又能活动身体，人们能从这类劳作中获得一种内在的愉悦感。”

11
00:01:25,990 --> 00:01:37,250
The internet has also been the place to turn to to buy craft kits which help you get started with your craft-making projects, such as candle making or macrame.
互联网也成了人们购买手工材料包的好去处，这些材料包能帮你开启各类手工项目，比如制作蜡烛或是编织挂毯。

12
00:01:37,250 --> 00:01:49,360
But many people are enjoying designing and making things from scratch and are doing it just for pleasure or to occupy their minds – and there’s evidence that it’s good for us as well.
不过也有很多人喜欢从零开始设计和制作物件，他们做这些只是为了消遣，或是让自己有事可做——而且有证据表明，手工制作对我们自己也大有裨益。

13
00:01:49,360 --> 00:02:03,220
According to research commissioned by BBC Arts, even the briefest time spent on a creative pastime such as painting, pottery or playing the piano, has an impact on our wellbeing and emotions.
英国广播公司艺术频道委托开展的一项研究显示，哪怕只是花很短的时间投入一项创意消遣活动，比如绘画、陶艺或是弹钢琴，都会对我们的身心健康和情绪状态产生积极影响。

14
00:02:03,220 --> 00:02:16,170
The survey of around 50,000 people found being creative can help avoid stress, free up mind space and improve self-development, which helps build self-esteem.
这项涵盖约5万人的调查发现，发挥创造力有助于缓解压力、放空思绪、促进自我成长，而这些都能帮助提升自信心。

15
00:02:16,170 --> 00:02:24,520
So, if you’re looking for the perfect tonic for your stressed-out life, maybe now’s the time to get creative.
所以，如果你正在为自己压力满满的生活寻找一剂良方，或许现在就是动手发挥创造力的好时机。
